From ec35017691e17f4afc6f44815003da5a93b16b39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arc <a@b.c>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:05:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arc: 0001-view-video-tool (read a local video file into the
 model's input)

Adds a `view_video` tool mirroring `view_image`, the protocol types it needs,
and a config override for input modalities.

- `InputModality::Video` and `FunctionCallOutputContentItem::InputVideo`.
  The wire tag is `video_url`, not `input_video`: the Responses API has no
  official video content part, and OpenAI-compatible servers that do accept
  video key on the chat-style tag. The Rust name stays aligned with its
  siblings via `#[serde(rename)]`.
- `model_input_modalities` config. Codex cannot read modality metadata from an
  OpenAI-compatible `/v1/models`, so an unknown slug falls back to text+image
  and the video gate can never open. Threaded through `ModelInfoOverrides`,
  which every model-info resolution passes through -- setting it only on
  `Config` silently does nothing.
- `strip_video_when_unsupported`, matching the existing image/audio strippers.
  Without it, video left in history after a model switch reaches the API and
  fails there, with an error that does not name the cause.
- Token estimate for `video_url` parts in the context manager, next to the
  image and audio ones: frame count and display size from the mp4/mov header,
  ceil(frames / 2) x (ceil(w / 32) * ceil(h / 32) + 16) tokens, the tool's
  `max_frames` / `max_tokens_per_frame` hints not applied (the server bills the
  container's frames); an unreadable container keeps its raw size. Without it a
  video counted as base64 bytes / 4 and the post-sampling check compacted right
  after the call: a 450 KB recording came out at ~152k tokens, ~1.7k on sglang.
- `Feature::ViewVideo`, under development and off by default.
